------------------------------------------------------------------------------
Bundled YARA rule packs (src/Tamp.McpScanner/rules/**)
------------------------------------------------------------------------------

The YARA rule files under src/Tamp.McpScanner/rules/ are derived from the
Cisco mcp-scanner project:

    https://github.com/cisco-ai-defense/mcp-scanner
    Copyright 2025 Cisco Systems, Inc. and its affiliates
    Licensed under the Apache License, Version 2.0

The files under rules/common/ are verbatim copies of Cisco's rules, retaining
their original authorship (`author = "Cisco"`).

The files under rules/dotnet/, rules/typescript/, and rules/python/ are
MODIFICATIONS of the corresponding Cisco rules: the detection patterns are
Cisco's; the Tamp Project has added per-stack negative conditions to suppress
false positives caused by idiomatic phrasing of that technology stack. Modified
files note the change in their header and in their `author` metadata. No change
is made to the threat detection itself — only to what counts as a match against
ordinary, legitimate tool descriptions for that stack.

